  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering women small-holder farmers in the rice value chain in Tanzania</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women do 70% of the work in rice production in Tanzania but see little of the income.  There is a growing internal demand for good quality rice yet 20% of rice is imported.  A 2 year pilot showed how linking women farmers directly with processors in a village-based contract farming model led to a 67% increase in price and almost doubled profit.  This project will scale up this model by supporting 25,000 women to form producer groups to have contracts directly with processors.  They will provide women with inputs and credit to improve quality and yields leading to increased income into their own pockets.</narrative>
  </description>
